    {
      "id": "v1/5nn4_SC2_A_1017__top1/r02/G2",
      "evidence_sha256": "c18d19ec2458335dbb22147595f22fbc2f102a9666d1f74c852d7297c46f5317",
      "assessment": "R2 G2 reads incumbent-minus-latest +0.01318 as positive treatment response while every latest-minus-incumbent quartile is negative, then explains the arithmetic with a nonexistent cancelling exchange. The correct result is 4.16490 versus incumbent 4.17808. H1 [6,6,5,5] and H2 [5,6,6,5] are meaningful location contrasts, but their premise is wrong; selected H1 gives R3 Mean 4.16103.",
      "decision_update": "Before interpreting heterogeneity, verify that the weighted quartile means equal the pooled mean in the same direction and common-valid population. Separate descriptive concentration from an invented noise floor. Keep paired location contrasts, but prefer their actual same-parent results over a narrative built from a sign reversal.",
      "counterexample_or_limitation": "All four equally sized quartile means cannot be negative while their identically oriented pooled mean is positive; that contradiction should trigger a sign/selection audit, not a causal account. The unselected H2 has no sampled affinity outcome and must remain unevaluated.",
