      "assessment": "R2 G3 correctly reads the current 0.01687 incumbent advantage and requests r01-to-latest directly, obtaining -0.0000304. Yet it retains the public-memory fiction that the 0.72 loss cancels, mixes a maximum of about 0.00195 with a mean in H1's falsifier, and calls the terminal comparison a same-parent isolation despite changed restart parents. Proposed H1 [6,6,5,6] and H2 [5,5,5,6] are not selected.",
      "decision_update": "Use typed metric names including aggregation, units, state and step range in falsifiers. Verify source/restart lineage before calling a contrast isolated, and correct false prior public-memory claims when direct evidence contradicts them. A local terminal null supports lower priority within the observed region, not a universal inability to tune late guidance.",
      "counterexample_or_limitation": "The terminal displacement increased while the score scarcely changed, supporting a proxy-response question but not a proof of complete inertness. Neither proposed next schedule was executed in R3, so no eventual R3 group outcome can be assigned to these proposals.",
