      "evidence_sha256": "07ce47eea249d53171a96e33ff56875746547f1d8a869968914d3ce3dc9bde3f",
      "assessment": "R2 G4 requests explicit r00-to-r02 paired and subgroup evidence, correctly returning -0.00745675, but its final memory still labels the +0.003707 change from r01 as relative to r00 and repeats the reversed incumbent comparison. Its symmetric proposals [6,5,6,5] and [4,5,6,5] are both selected; R3 means 4.16217 and 4.10918 differ by +0.052994 in favor of the higher early tick.",
      "decision_update": "Keep the useful matched opposite-direction design while anchoring every quoted difference to its actual populations. Evaluate the contrast using all common identities and report both its mean and concentration; an unselected private agent must not assume sibling results before publication. Do not infer low-score assignment switching from aggregate switching alone.",
      "counterexample_or_limitation": "The observed 0.052994 same-wave contrast is dominated by a maximum +4.4206 and near-zero median, so it is evidence of concentrated sensitivity, not a broad monotone law. Small perturbations are demonstrably capable of large discrete outcome changes.",
